{"parentUuid":"22f28934-f1fe-45b6-a7c6-d84a16edc5ed","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"2663ffb1-1efa-4860-8b90-75febb6a5f0b","agentId":"a9bc91478f203aae9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The task comes from the coordinator, relaying Kemal; everything is in Turkish and the report must be short and plain Turkish.\n   - **Hard rules:**\n     - Work only in W = `C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE\\AUTOKITCH_COORDINATION\\worktrees\\claude-hat3-v8`. Scratch is S = `C:\\Users\\Kemal\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-Kemal-Desktop-Kemal-WEBS-TE\\f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8\\scratchpad`.\n     - No push, no coord commands.\n     - Commit model and animation separately with `git add <file>`. Every commit message ends with \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\".\n     - Do not touch the A-animation agent's files; it works in parallel.\n     - Every change goes into the chain as a new step (SIRA.md + zincir.py) and is verified byte-identical across two runs.\n   - **Request 1:** remove all 6 emergency stops from step 40. Done.\n   - **Request 2 (B model gaps):**\n     - (a) PU boards must be cut so each can actually be inserted; insulation volume and U value unchanged; PU stays invisible.\n     - (b) Real fasteners wherever a part has none: posts and ladder frames to the outer floor, evaporator brackets, cooling unit, electrical box, inner channels, heat-shield radiation sheet, station box, chain duct, and the floating channel.\n     - (c) Closed-end M8 rivet nuts with M8×16 bolts.\n     - (d) Re-route the evaporator cable away from ic_kanal_31.\n   - **Request 3:** regenerate the B animation (`b-montaj.html`) from the new model. No emergency-stop step, PU boards inserted one by one, fasteners into their own holes, checks 17–19 clean, \"model açığı\" count 0.\n   - **Coordinator additions:**\n     - Integrate `S\\gece2\\a3\\zincir_A_tamamla.py` as a chain step, and shorten the A→TOPPING M8×16 bolts to M8×10.\n     - Kemal's animation feedback:\n       - Plain-Turkish step texts with no raw part names.\n       - A fixed legend: yellow = PU, orange = part being fitted, RED = weld/spot weld (stays red), blue = fasteners, green = adhesive/silicone.\n       - Name the black boxes seen in screenshot 118.\n       - Show how the left side sheet is held (köşebent + spot welds).\n       - Insulated panels: PU glued, inner sheets with bent flanges and rivets, joints sealed with silicone, nothing appearing to float.\n       - Put this in the shared player; rebuild the A and single-drawer pages with it.\n     - After the 46–50 commit, write \"MODEL HAZIR: <path>\" to `S\\gece2\\DURUM.md`.\n     - Latest: the TOPPING agent committed 28b1bdf (chain 37–50 rebuilt, page ?v=9s, main GLB = v9s). Do not make a conflicting commit. If needed, add step 51 on top of v9s for the two reported collisions, then finish the B animation and the A/drawer rebuild on the final model and update DURUM.md.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GLB patch chain (`zincir.py` ADIMLAR list, SON, byte verification over two work folders).\n   - Libraries and existing tools:\n     - m8kit Glb (`bilesen`, `donustur`, `sil_b`, `ekle_dugum`, `etiket_b`); appended triangles only appear as components after save and reload.\n     - sac_ent: `Karsi.delik_ac` (manifold boolean holes, `vida_mi` clearance), `Ham` raw node writer, `sikistir`.\n     - manifold3d booleans, `trim_by_plane`, `hull_points`.\n     - govde_denetim_dogru collision audit; VTK can give false positives on open meshes, so OCC verification counts.\n   - Repair of open PU meshes by snapping to a 0.01 mm grid.\n   - New nodes `B_KASA__pu_dolgu` and `B_BAGLANTI__paslanmaz`, needed because coplanar cut faces made the audit merge touching parts.\n   - meshopt lossless compression: `node meshopt_kucult.mjs <raw> <page> --idx seq`, using node at `C:\\Program Files\\Adobe\\Adobe Creative Cloud Experience\\libs\\node.exe`.\n   - Animation pipeline in `S\\gece2\\b4\\anim`: cikar_b.py → bil_cikar.py → mk_parca.py → b4_parca.py → yap_montaj.py (builds b4_montaj.py from b3_montaj.py + plan_v4.py) → b4_montaj.py → yap_cikti.py → b4_cikti.py, which writes `W\\otonom\\hat3d\\v3\\b_montaj\\b_montaj.(glb|json)`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`W\\arastirma\\_uretec\\h3\\yama_v9\\45_acil_stop_kaldir.py`** (committed 47864e2). Inputs v9l + v9g, output v9m. Deletes the ACIL_STOP__sari/siyah/kirmizi nodes, meshes and materials, remaps node indices, and restores the 10 pockets from the v9g components with a volume check.\n   - **`46_b_pu_levha.py`** (v9m→v9n):\n     - pu_arka_yuksek/alcak split at z=−805 into arka and ön layers.\n     - pu_sol split into main board, arka_serit (x≥761, z≤−805) and kose_alt/ust 1–3 (analytic `kose_alt`/`kose_ust`, pay 3.75).\n     - tk_depo kose pieces merged into `tk_depo_kose_dolgu`.\n     - pu_taban_0 gets Ø25 through-holes at the 10 SASE_M8 positions plus `pu_taban_tapa_*` plugs.\n     - Fillers and plugs go to `B_KASA__pu_dolgu`; the script checks volume is unchanged.\n   - **`47_b_baglanti.py`** and **`veri/bag47.py`** (v9n→v9o):\n     - bag47 builders: `fhs`, `pul`, `somun`, `civata4762`, `civata7380`, `kaynak_somunu`, `percin_somun_kapali`, `kor_percin`. Each element dict now carries `n` (axis).\n     - Pre-pass repairs open PU components.\n     - `Karsi(haric_onek=(\"B_KASA__pu\",))`; PU pockets are cut separately via `onar` and boolean.\n     - Groups:\n       - A: post feet (end plate, 2× DIN 929 M5 weld nut, M5×16 bolt and washer from below, Ø9.5 access hole).\n       - B: evaporator brackets, with a lug added to the top brackets.\n       - C: cooling-unit rail ends (M4 bolt into a closed-end M4 rivet nut, or a nut under the floor).\n       - D: electrical plate, 6 FHS-M5 studs.\n       - E: station box with 2 U-brackets.\n       - F: chain duct with 2 L-brackets (rivets plus FHS studs).\n       - G: radiation sheet, 12 FHS-M4-18.\n       - H: inner channels now use blind rivets Ø4/Ø3.2 (spacer bush where there is a gap).\n       - H2: B_KABLO channels, Ø4 blind rivets.\n       - J: closed-end M8 rivet nuts (+4 mm solid end) and bolts shortened to M8×16, including the A/TOPPING base bolts.\n       - K: evaporator cable shifted +3.93 y with tapered ends.\n     - `delikle()` drills brackets and clamps for the fasteners that pass through them; `isabet()` adds an open-mesh prism test.\n   - **`48_a_tamamla.py`** (v9o→v9p): the A agent's script plus A5 (A→TOPPING M8×16 → ×10). A1 bolt search range set to 775.9–800.1.\n   - **`49_b_ic_kabuk.py`** (v9p→v9q):\n     - F1: ic_taban rear flange goes up behind ic_arka.\n     - F4: ic_sol_duvar bottom, rear and top flanges bend to the food side.\n     - F6: bölme flanges 12 mm outward, notched around obstacles.\n     - 213 DIN 7337 Ø4 rivets. Rivets must hit their own flange and avoid other flanges (FLM).\n     - PU pockets cut via onar; flanges joined to their owning sheet after save and reload; small detached pieces are dropped.\n     - No F2 or F3 flanges.\n   - **`50_sikilastir.py`** (v9q→v9r): removes degenerate triangles and unused vertices and remaps the kat/mek/kpk extras.\n   - **`zincir.py`**: steps 45–50 added; a step's stale output is deleted before the step runs. **`SIRA.md`**: sections for steps 45 and 46–50 added.\n   - **Page files:**\n     - `W\\otonom\\hat\\makine_v3_8.html`: ?v=9r in my commit (TOPPING later set 9s).\n     - `mekanizma_v3_8.json` / `parca_kutulari.json`: ACIL_STOP removed, B_BAGLANTI birim added, new PU pieces added.\n   - **Shared player** `W\\otonom\\hat\\ist_montaj\\montaj-oynatici.js` (committed by the TOPPING agent in 79bb581):\n     - Legend, red kaynak/punta materials, blue fasteners, green yapistirici.\n     - `D.sehpa` flag; `D.aciklama` / `D.istisna_metin`; `model_acigi` count in the check summary.\n   - **Uncommitted page changes:**\n     - `a-montaj.html` and `cekmece-montaj.html` now load montaj-oynatici.js?v=1 and have updated legends.\n     - `a_montaj.json` and `cekmece_montaj.json` have `aciklama` / `istisna_metin` added.\n     - `b-montaj.html`: v4 tag, new lead and foot texts, loads montaj-oynatici.js.\n     - `b_montaj.glb/json` were regenerated from the old v9r.\n   - **Animation scripts in `S\\gece2\\b4\\anim`:**\n     - `mk_parca.py` builds `b4_parca.py`:\n       - Reads bil_r.pkl, ENT, and the E46/E47/E49 ent jsons from `..\\is1`.\n       - Uses `parca_govde_blok.py` for body matching (exact box, then containing box, then contained box).\n       - Splits `zemin_conta` and `sogutma_ust_sac` into separate parts and removes acil_stop.\n     - `plan_v4.py`:\n       - TR naming (`ad_tr`), adhesive films (`yapistirici`/`yapistir`), spot welds from `puntalar_B.json` (`puntala`).\n       - Stud and host logic (`STUD`, `ev_sahibi` with `sac_once`), fastener groups (`GRUP`, `GDOKUN` including b_ sheet parts).\n       - f1 rivets wait for g_teknik_sol_duvar; `baglantilari_tamamla`; `adim_sonu`.\n       - Order: taban with plugs → alt köşe fillers and köşebent → arka panel bench assembly from behind → sol yan → sol PU → ic_arka → ic_sol_duvar → bölmeler (YAN=36; teknik wall ('on',(3,0,0))) → teknik step (grubu 'ust' → elektrik 'on' → zincir 'ust') → sağ yan → istasyon → evaporatörler → kanallar → tahrik → ic_tavan + PU tavan bench sandwich → ısı kalkanı → üst köşebent + fillers → iskelet (feet bolts) → tavan → ön çerçeve → raylar → çekmeceler → depo.\n       - Fastener `tak` travel: 22 mm for bolts, 7 mm for others.\n     - `yap_montaj.py` (yon_sec records every candidate in `tum`), `yap_cikti.py`:\n       - Exemptions: decoration (yap_/punta_); rivet/PEM/bush in its own hole for every part touching its final bbox (cables excluded).\n       - Build-frame check skips yap_/punta_.\n       - MATAD adds punta and yapistirici.\n       - Kaynak dikişleri, puntalar, yapıştırıcı ve silikon tanımlı \"DEKOR\" parçalardır.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Step 45 IndexError on empty components:** wrapped in try/except.\n   - **PU meshes not manifold:** b3 extraction misassigned shared faces. Fixed by using m8kit components and snap-repairing at 0.01 mm.\n   - **Hull-sweep regions produced zero-volume fins:** switched to analytic half-space regions.\n   - **Split pieces merged into one component in the audit:** moved to a separate node.\n   - **Stud/nut collisions inside cable channels:** first M3 and spacer fallbacks, then clamps, finally replaced all channel fasteners with blind rivets so they do not block other parts' paths.\n   - **OCC tessellation cache:** `shape.copy()` needed before coarse tessellation.\n   - **ADIM 48:** A1 bolt not found after my M8×16 change; search range adjusted.\n   - **ADIM 49:**\n     - F2/F3/F5 flanges collided with PU paths → removed; F4 redesigned to the food side.\n     - Flanged sheet split into pieces → fixed by connected flange boxes and dropping small fragments.\n     - Rivets overlapped other flanges → FLM check added.\n     - Rivets sat in a flange notch → own-flange check added.\n     - Sheets not found after `delik_ac` → save and reload before union.\n     - PU repair failed after step-47 pockets → PU repair moved into 47 and pockets cut via onar.\n   - **pkill does not exist in this shell.**\n   - **Python unicode escape error** writing DURUM.md → used printf.\n   - **Animation plan collisions:** fixed one by one — adhesive films removed from blockers, weld-nut host restricted, reordering, bench assemblies, PU taban plugs, YAN 36, teknik wall YAN 3, foam-cap exemptions, B_KABLO channel parts no longer excluded as fasteners.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Model audits:**\n     - Last full audit (v9r4): B 5 collisions, ELK 0, A 0.\n     - Targeted audit (v9r5): 3 left.\n       - Two are false positives: B_KASA__sac[90] ↔ CEK_K1_lahm_5 celik[3] and ↔ ELK_DOLAP kablo_sinyal[82]. OCC 0, prism ∩ solid volume 0.000, nearest distance 10.05 / 3.19 mm.\n       - The third, conta 0.064 mm, already existed from step 44.\n     - Conclusion: no step 51 needed; noted in DURUM.md.\n   - **Chain determinism:** 45–50 byte-identical across two runs (is1/is2/is3).\n   - **Animation (on the old v9r):**\n     - Plan problems 0, unscheduled 0, build-frame problems 0, pop-ins 0, model gaps 0.\n     - Path collisions 90, all rivet or spacer moves through cables:\n       - Rivets vs CEK cables: 63.\n       - Rivets vs evaporator cable: 10.\n       - Spacers vs evaporator cable: 6.\n       - Spacers vs power cable: 5.\n       - Rivets vs power cable: 5.\n       - Spacer vs rivet: 1.\n     - Havada: 56, mainly bench-welded or with-host items: weld nuts, rivet nuts, istasyon fasteners.\n   - **Black boxes in screenshot 118:**\n     - Small one = PTFE takoz under the heat shield.\n     - Big box on the rear wall = gider geçişi silikonu (now green).\n     - Cylinders = step motors.\n\n6. All user messages (task + coordinator relays):\n   - **Original task:** \"AUTOKITCH — MODEL DÜZELTME: ACİL STOPLARI KALDIR + B'NİN MODEL AÇIKLARI + B ANİMASYONUNU GÜNCELLE. Türkçe. Hedef ~2 saat. Kemal: 'her şeyi yap, en son şu eksik deme.'\"\n     - Includes points 1–3 and the DENETİM requirements.\n     - Server start command if it is down: `Start-Process python -ArgumentList '-m','http.server','8766','--bind','127.0.0.1','--directory','\"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE\\AUTOKITCH_COORDINATION\\worktrees\"' -WindowStyle Hidden`.\n     - \"COMMIT: model ve animasyon ayrı (git add <dosya>), mesaj sonu 'Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>'. Push/coord YOK. Paralelde A montaj animasyonu yapan bir ajan var … onun dosyalarına dokunma. RAPOR: kısa sade Türkçe.\"\n   - **Coordinator EK:** add the A agent's 4 fixes (zincir_A_tamamla.py) as a new step; A–TOPPING M8×16 → M8×10; report the last raw GLB name.\n   - **Coordinator, Kemal's B feedback:** plain texts with no raw names; legend (sarı PU, turuncu takılan, KIRMIZI kaynak kalıcı, mavi vida); identify the black boxes; show how the left side sheet is held with real joints; put the same in the shared player and rebuild the A and drawer pages.\n   - **Coordinator, Kemal:** \"o saclar o yalıtımlara nasıl takılıyor, havada duruyor gibiler\" — PU glued (green legend), inner sheet bent flanges with rivets or screws, food-side joint silicone, no floating sheet; apply to B and the shared generator.\n   - **Coordinator ACİL:** stop and finish step 45 only (with check, meshopt, ?v, browser, commit) within 15 minutes, report \"acil stoplar kalktı, commit X\" plus the remaining time for 46–49. Done: 47864e2.\n   - **Coordinator:** continue 46–50 (check, byte verification, page, commit), then the B animation with feedback; rebuild A and drawer with the shared player; write \"MODEL HAZIR: <yol>\" to DURUM.md right after the 46–50 commit (TOPPING agent waiting).\n   - **Coordinator check:** 46–50 not committed and no MODEL HAZIR line; finish those first or report what is blocking. Done afterwards: 5aaaf36 + MODEL HAZIR.\n   - **Coordinator DİKKAT:** the TOPPING agent produced chain 37–50 byte-identical and committed 28b1bdf, ?v=9s (main GLB = v9s); do not make a conflicting commit. My remaining model work: on v9s, a new step 51_b_duzelt.py for the 2 collisions (B_KASA__sac[90] ↔ CEK_K1_lahm_5 10 mm; ↔ ELK_DOLAP kablo 3.7 mm; conta 0.064 ignored), verify chain 37–51, main GLB + meshopt + ?v, commit; then finish the B animation and the A/drawer rebuild on that final model; write to DURUM.md.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Tell the coordinator that the two collisions are false positives, so there is no step 51 and v9s stays the model (already in DURUM.md). If the coordinator still insists, a 51 step would have no geometric effect.\n   - Rebuild the B animation on v9s (`S\\gece2\\t3\\is_A\\hat3_v9r.glb`): copy to `anim\\hat3_v9r.glb` or point the pipeline at it, then re-extract (cikar_b, bil_cikar, mk_parca, b4_parca) and run b4_montaj and b4_cikti.\n   - Remove the remaining 90 path collisions: rivets and spacers crossing cables. Options: shorter travel (about 3 mm) for rivets and spacers inside channels, or pull cables after the rivets.\n   - Review the havada list and explain it on the page.\n   - Check in the browser that b-montaj, a-montaj and cekmece-montaj open with a clean console and the legend shows.\n   - Commit the animation separately: b-montaj.html, b_montaj.glb/json, a-montaj.html, cekmece-montaj.html, a_montaj.json, cekmece_montaj.json. montaj-oynatici.js is already committed by TOPPING; check whether it differs.\n   - Final short Turkish report:\n     - Commits 47864e2 and 5aaaf36.\n     - Raw GLB and DURUM.md note.\n     - Step 51 not needed, with the reason.\n     - Animation check figures.\n     - What the black boxes in screenshot 118 are.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   The last pipeline run (old v9r) finished: plan problems 0; path collisions 90, all rivets or spacers vs cables (CEK_K*_kablo, evap_kablo, guc_kablo); build frames 0; pop-ins 0; model gaps 0; havada 56. Before that I checked the coordinator's step-51 request and wrote the false-positive note to DURUM.md, so no step 51 will be added. Next is regenerating the animation on v9s and fixing the cable collisions in `plan_v4.py`. Fastener travel is set in `baglantilari_tamamla`:\n   `P[a]['eks'] = tuple(eks); tt_ = tak(a, tt_, 0.4, 22.0 if P[a]['etur'] == 'civata' else 7.0) + 0.05`\n   The exemptions are in `yap_cikti.py`, where cables are deliberately excluded.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Per the coordinator's latest instruction: \"Sonra B animasyonunu (ve A/çekmece yeniden üretimini) bu son modelle tamamla. DURUM.md'ye yaz.\"\n   1. Point the animation pipeline at v9s (`S\\gece2\\t3\\is_A\\hat3_v9r.glb`) and re-extract the parts.\n   2. In plan_v4.py, cut travel for rivets and spacers inside channels to about 3 mm (or schedule them before the cables are pulled) so the 90 cable collisions go away.\n   3. Rerun b4_montaj and b4_cikti.\n   4. Check the three pages in the browser at http://127.0.0.1:8766/claude-hat3-v8/otonom/hat/… with a clean console.\n   5. Commit the animation files separately and update DURUM.md.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\Kemal\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-Kemal-Desktop-Kemal-WEBS-TE\\f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"01c42c3e-2529-4504-9893-325a3908de4f","timestamp":"2026-10-04T17:31:52.191Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE\\AUTOKITCH_COORDINATION\\worktrees\\claude-hat3-v8","sessionId":"f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"crystalline-crunching-moonbeam"}
{"parentUuid":"01c42c3e-2529-4504-9893-325a3908de4f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a9bc91478f203aae9","attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-Kemal-Desktop-Kemal-WEBS-TE\\f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8\\scratchpad\\gece2\\b4\\anim\\yap_cikti.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-Kemal-Desktop-Kemal-WEBS-TE\\f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8\\scratchpad\\gece2\\b4\\anim\\yap_cikti.py","content":"import io\ns = io.open('../../b3/b3_cikti.py', encoding='utf-8').read()\nR = [\n(\"sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(HERE, '..', 'cekmece')); sys.path.insert(0, HERE)\", \"sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(HERE, '..', '..', 'cekmece')); sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(HERE, '..', '..', 'b3')); sys.path.insert(0, HERE)\"),\n(\"D = pickle.load(open('plan_b3.pkl', 'rb'))\", \"D = pickle.load(open('plan_b4.pkl', 'rb'))\"),\n(\"\"\"for ck in D['CEKD']:\n    har(ck + '_kayis', ck + '_kasnak',\"\"\", \"\"\"# yapıştırıcı filmi / punta noktaları / kaynak dikişleri birleşme anında yerinde belirir; yol denetiminde engel sayılmaz (levha ya da sac yüzünde)\nDEKOR = [a for a in P if a.startswith(('yap_', 'punta_'))]\nfor d in DEKOR:\n    for b in P:\n        if b != d: HARIC[tuple(sorted((d, b)))] = 'yapıştırıcı filmi / punta noktası (yüzeyde, birleşme anında belirir)'\n# kör perçin (sıkılmış hâliyle modelde: uç şişkin) ve PEM saplama (baskıyla oturur) kendi deliğinden geçer: son konumda değdiği sac / kanal / levha ile çifti beyanlı\nLOa_ = {a: P[a]['V'].min(0) for a in P}; HIa_ = {a: P[a]['V'].max(0) for a in P}\nfor a in P:\n    et = P[a].get('etur')\n    if not (a.startswith('b_') and (et in ('percin', 'saplama', 'percin_somun') or a.endswith('_burc'))): continue\n    for b in P:\n        if b == a or P[b]['tur'] == 'kablo' or b.startswith(('b_', 'kaynak_', 'punta_', 'yap_')) and not (b.startswith('b_') and (P[b].get('etur') in ('percin', 'pul', 'saplama', 'sac') or not P[b].get('etur'))): continue\n        if np.all(HIa_[b] >= LOa_[a] - 0.3) and np.all(LOa_[b] <= HIa_[a] + 0.3):\n            HARIC[tuple(sorted((a, b)))] = 'kör perçin / PEM saplama / aralık burcu kendi deliğinde: gövde düz girer, perçin ucu sıkılınca şişer (model sıkılmış hâli) · saplama baskıyla oturur'\nfor ck in D['CEKD']:\n    har(ck + '_kayis', ck + '_kasnak',\"\"\"),\n(\"            if P[b].get('sac') == a: continue\", \"            if P[b].get('sac') == a or b.startswith(('yap_', 'punta_')): continue\"),\n(\"MATAD = ['sac', 'kapak', 'profil', 'kaynak',\", \"MATAD = ['punta', 'yapistirici', 'sac', 'kapak', 'profil', 'kaynak',\"),\n(\"\"\"vida_kayit('sase_civata', 'ISO 4762 M8', (0, -1, 0), 'dış taban Ø9 + pul', 'M8 kapalı uçlu perçin somun (şase üst duvarı)', -120.0, -yb.min(), 10, 'perçin somun gövdesi: y %.1f … 120 (iç diş)' % yb.min())\"\"\",\n \"\"\"vida_kayit('sase_civata', 'ISO 4762 M8 × 16', (0, -1, 0), 'dış taban Ø15,5 + pul', 'M8 kapalı uçlu perçin somun (şase üst duvarı, iç diş dibi y 107,5)', -124.5, -107.5, 10, 'kapalı uç: cıvata ucu diş dibinin %.1f mm üstünde' % (uc('sase_civata', (0, -1, 0)) * -1 - 107.5))\"\"\"),\n(\"HAVADA = sorted(a for a, (tl, l) in TEM.items() if not l and not a.endswith('_ara'))\", \"HAVADA = sorted(a for a, (tl, l) in TEM.items() if not l and not a.endswith('_ara') and not P[a].get('ev') and not P[a].get('tezgah'))   # üretimde preslenen / kaynaklanan ve tezgâhta bağlanan elemanlar ev sahibiyle birlikte gelir\"),\n(\"DEN = dict(adim=len(D['ADIM']),\", \"DEN = dict(model_acigi=sum(1 for k, v in HARIC.items() if v.startswith('MODEL AÇIĞI')), adim=len(D['ADIM']),\"),\n(\"OUTJ = dict(surum='b_montaj_v3', ist='B', tarih='4 Eki 2026', kaynak='hat3_v9l.glb (zincir 00–44) · B gövdesi h3_b_sac_v1 (açınım) + ana model · üretim: b3_montaj.py',\",\n \"OUTJ = dict(surum='b_montaj_v4', ist='B', tarih='4 Eki 2026', kaynak='hat3_v9r.glb (zincir 00–50) · B gövdesi h3_b_sac_v1 (açınım) + ana model · üretim: b4_montaj.py', sehp